\b0\fs24 SimpleImageFilter is a filter service which converts IFF (Interchange File Format) images to TIFF, allowing OpenStep applications to load and display IFF images. 
\b SimpleImageFilter_main.m
\b0  shows how one might create a filter service; 
\b iffToTiff.m
\b0  contains mostly uninteresting code that does the actual image conversion.\
\
Note that this program is not meant to be a complete IFF to TIFF converter; it lacks many features, ignores many IFF chunks, doesn't recognize all IFF types, and probably has a few bugs. It's simply provided as an example of a filter service, and as a tool with which developers can check to see if their applications use NSImage in a way that allows them to load images reachable through filter services. If you install this service in your 
\b ~/Library/Services
\b0  directory, you should be able to drag and open 
\b .iff
\b0  image files in any OpenStep application which imports images. A sample file (
\b SampleImage.iff
\b0 ) is provided for testing purposes.\
\
There are some tricky issues in creating a filter service:\

\pard\tx960\tx1920\tx2880\tx3840\tx4800\tx5760\tx6720\tx7680\tx8640\tx9600\fi-160\li160\fc0\cf0 · The project is an Application, not Bundle, allowing the standard makefiles to create an .exe instead of .dll on Windows\
· Makefile.postamble specifies that the wrapper extension should be ".service", not ".app" (see APP_WRAPPER_EXTENSION)\
· Makefile.postamble clears PROJTYPE_LDFLAGS on NEXTSTEP to avoid giving the executable an icon section. This way Workspace will not create an app tile when the service is launched.\
· We specify ".iff" and ".IFF" as extensions, as file names on Windows can come in all upper case\

